title: 'Q4, fact: Which client code and client unit tests still assume the retired ''all'' object, and why do those tests still pass?'
pid: 4279bc86-757e-479f-92f7-64666ba6d84d
body: |2-
  Key: Must name: the code that strips 'all' ('skg--processed-leaves-below' in Emacs and its Neovim mirror, and the AI reader's 'ALL_TOKEN'), and the unit tests 'tests/elisp/test-skg-processed.el' and 'tests/nvim/processed_spec.lua', which feed hand-written '(leaves 3 rel all)'; they pass because they never reach a server. Wrong: saying no client code mentions 'all', or that those tests fail.
  Where, as left: drawn: to Claude > "2026-11-13: Part 3 is built ..." (For Cleo, fourth bullet)
  Why asked: Cleo, part 4: 'client tests that still send the old form'
  Scores, Haiku 1-3 then Sonnet 1-3 (R right, W wrong, - not said): as left RRRRRR, tended ------.
